C++20 <map>: operator[] insert + access.

Reclassified CORE -> KNOWNBUG by the member-typedef conformance fix
([temp.inst]/1-2, [dcl.typedef]).  Previously this passed only because the
non-conformant *truncated* std::map had its operations havoc'd (symex executed
none of the real container; the property was vacuous).  The fix makes the front
end conformant and symex now executes the REAL std::map / _Rb_tree machinery.

Current layer (2026-07-15 evening): this exact program verifies fully
UNBOUNDED under --cpp11 after the delegating-piecewise-constructor chain
was fixed (cpp11_piecewise_delegating_ctor, cpp11_static_cast_base_rref,
and the earlier cpp11_* piecewise tests are all CORE, and
'm[1]=42; assert(m[1]==42)' verifies in ~1.6s bounded).  Under --cpp20
the headers construct the node through a DIFFERENT chain
(std::construct_at / _S_construct, C++20 constexpr allocator_traits):
the stored key byte is again malloc garbage (trace: storage[0]=64), so
the read-back re-inserts and the unbounded tree walk diverges in the
_Rb_tree_decrement model.  NEXT: peel the C++20 construct_at chain the
same way.  The FRONT-END chain is now complete: the free-function-template
new-initializer pack expansion (cpp11_construct_at_pack_args), the void
constexpr wrapper deferral (cpp11_void_constexpr_wrapper_defer), and the
trailing-return decltype-over-pack-new deduction
(cpp11_construct_at_decltype_return) are all fixed and CORE.  With them,
--cpp20 instantiates std::construct_at and runs std::map's piecewise node
construction (the key is stored correctly).  The REMAINING reason this
test does not pass is a bounded-model-checking SOLVER-SCALING limit on the
fully-inlined C++20 container: without an unwind bound the _Rb_tree
machinery builds a formula the SAT backend cannot discharge in the time
budget (at --unwind 5 the equation is built in ~6.5min and the solver
then runs out of resources).  This is not a front-end conformance issue:
the identical program verifies unbounded under --cpp11 (the C++11 headers
inline less).  Reclassify to CORE if/when the container machinery is
made tractable (a lighter model, or bounded --unwind with a coarser
property).

Second-tier verification-PERFORMANCE item, not a conformance one; the previous
"pass" was unsound.  Reclassify back to CORE once symex is tractable on the real
container.
See doc/architectural/cpp-class-template-instantiation-plan.md.
